---
import CaseContents from "./CaseContents.astro";
---
<article class="ck-case">
  <header><div class="meta case-meta"><span class="case-meta__client-full">Carrabba’s Italian Grill / Bloomin’ Brands</span><span class="case-meta__client-short">Carrabba’s</span><span class="case-meta__highlight">40% faster access</span></div><div class="intro"><div><p>Content strategy &amp; UX architecture</p><h1>From table<br />to kitchen.</h1></div><div><p class="lede">A restaurant brand became a practical cooking resource—built for the moment someone needs to make dinner, not make a reservation.</p><dl><div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Senior UX Strategist</dd></div><div><dt>Result</dt><dd>40% faster time-to-recipe</dd></div></dl></div></div></header>
  <CaseContents links={[{"href": "#case-section-1", "label": "The brief"}, {"href": "#case-section-2", "label": "Content architecture"}, {"href": "#case-section-3", "label": "Reading experience"}, {"href": "#case-section-4", "label": "Brand details"}, {"href": "#case-section-5", "label": "Outcome"}]} />
  <figure class="hero"><img src="/images/carrabbas_hero.webp" alt="Carrabba’s restaurant kitchen" loading="eager" /></figure>
  <section class="opening" id="case-section-1" tabindex="-1"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Reframing the job</p><h2>Teach the technique.<br />Earn the return visit.</h2></div><div><p>Testing with home cooks showed two distinct mindsets: experienced cooks looked for techniques and ingredients; novices looked for a successful outcome. Neither group needed a promotional maze.</p><p>The platform separated discovery from execution, organizing content around how people actually cook.</p></div></section>
  <section class="blueprint" id="case-section-2" tabindex="-1"><figure><img src="/images/carrabbas01.webp" alt="Carrabba’s Kitchen wireframes" loading="lazy" /></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / Content architecture</p><h2>Many ways in.<br />One clear way through.</h2><p>Popular, recent, and topic-led paths made discovery feel open without forcing a linear journey. Action-led titles set a practical expectation before the first tap.</p><figure><img src="/images/carrabbas02.webp" alt="Carrabba’s Kitchen mobile recipe discovery" loading="lazy" /></figure></div></section>
  <figure class="mobile-field"><img src="/images/carrabbas03.webp" alt="Carrabba’s Kitchen across mobile screens" loading="lazy" /></figure>
  <section class="reading" id="case-section-3" tabindex="-1"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Made for the kitchen</p><h2>Read, cook,<br />look back.</h2><p>Recipe pages used a vertical, scroll-optimized flow with large targets, clear ingredient hierarchy, and minimal chrome—so the interface stayed useful with one hand occupied.</p></div><div class="reading__images"><figure><img src="/images/carrabbas04.webp" alt="Carrabba’s Kitchen mobile interface collection" loading="lazy" /></figure><figure><img src="/images/carrabbas05.webp" alt="Carrabba’s Kitchen chef portrait" loading="lazy" /></figure><figure><img src="/images/carrabbas06.webp" alt="Carrabba’s pasta recipe" loading="lazy" /></figure></div></section>
  <section class="warmth" id="case-section-4" tabindex="-1"><figure><img src="/images/carrabbas07.webp" alt="Carrabba’s family food moment" loading="lazy" /></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / Brand in the details</p><h2>Warmth without clutter.</h2><p>Food photography carried the appetite appeal. Carrabba’s Tableside type handled the brand moments; clean, legible body type did the practical work. The result felt unmistakably Carrabba’s—and still easy to use at a glance.</p></div></section>
  <section class="outcome" id="case-section-5" tabindex="-1"><div><p class="eyebrow">05 / Outcome</p><h2>A system the<br />content team could keep cooking with.</h2><div class="stats"><div><b>40%</b><span>faster time-to-recipe</span></div><div><b>28%</b><span>more mobile session depth</span></div><div><b>3 weeks</b><span>to independent publishing</span></div></div></div><figure><img src="/images/carrabbas08.webp" alt="Carrabba’s Kitchen responsive publishing system" loading="lazy" /></figure></section>
</article>
<style>
.ck-case{--green:#0f4828;--lime:#a8c92b;--cream:#f7f2e9;--ink:#17251b;--line:#c8c9b9;background:var(--cream);color:var(--ink);font-family:Manrope,Arial,sans-serif}.ck-case *{box-sizing:border-box}.ck-case figure,.ck-case p,.ck-case h1,.ck-case h2{margin:0}.ck-case img{display:block;height:100%;object-fit:cover;width:100%}header{padding:28px 4vw 88px}.meta{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);display:flex;font-size:11px;justify-content:space-between;letter-spacing:.08em;padding-bottom:15px;text-transform:uppercase}.intro,.opening,.blueprint,.reading,.warmth,.outcome{display:grid;gap:8vw;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr}.intro{align-items:end;padding-top:78px}.eyebrow,.intro>div>p:first-child{color:#47783b;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}.intro h1{font-size:clamp(72px,12vw,190px);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.09em;line-height:.78;margin-top:26px}.lede{font-size:clamp(19px,2vw,29px);letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:1.25}.intro dl{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:44px;padding-top:13px}.intro dl div{display:flex;font-size:12px;justify-content:space-between;margin:10px 0}.intro dt{color:#47783b}.intro dd{margin:0;text-align:right}.hero{height:min(55vw,830px)}.opening{padding:140px 4vw}.ck-case h2{font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,98px);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.075em;line-height:.9;margin-top:22px}.opening>div:last-child,.blueprint>div>p,.reading>div>p,.warmth p{align-self:end;color:#435c48;font-size:18px;line-height:1.5}.opening>div:last-child{display:grid;gap:22px}.blueprint{background:var(--green);color:#f5f2e9;padding:4vw}.blueprint>figure{aspect-ratio:1.45}.blueprint>div{display:grid;align-content:start;gap:26px}.blueprint .eyebrow{color:#c4e64d}.blueprint>div>p{color:#d7e3d6;max-width:480px}.blueprint>div figure{margin-top:30px;width:58%}.blueprint>div figure img{aspect-ratio:.72}.mobile-field{height:min(50vw,760px)}.reading{padding:140px 4vw}.reading>div:first-child{display:grid;align-content:start;gap:24px}.reading__images{display:grid;gap:16px;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.reading__images figure:first-child{grid-column:1/-1}.reading__images figure:first-child img{aspect-ratio:1.8}.reading__images figure:not(:first-child) img{aspect-ratio:.72}.warmth{background:#ded5c5;padding:4vw}.warmth figure{height:min(50vw,760px)}.warmth>div{align-self:end}.outcome{background:var(--green);color:#f5f2e9;padding:130px 4vw 0}.outcome .eyebrow{color:#c4e64d}.stats{border-top:1px solid #66915b;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);margin-top:80px}.stats div{border-right:1px solid #66915b;padding:18px 18px 42px 0}.stats div+div{padding-left:18px}.stats b{display:block;font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,90px);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.08em;line-height:.8}.stats span{display:block;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35;margin-top:18px;max-width:120px}.outcome figure{align-self:end}.outcome figure img{aspect-ratio:1.78}@media(max-width:760px){.intro,.opening,.blueprint,.reading,.warmth,.outcome{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:34px}.intro{padding-top:48px}.opening,.reading,.outcome{padding-top:82px;padding-bottom:82px}.blueprint>div figure{width:65%}.stats{grid-template-columns:1fr;margin-top:48px}.stats div,.stats div+div{border-bottom:1px solid #66915b;border-right:0;padding:18px 0 26px}.outcome figure{margin-bottom:-82px}.reading__images figure:first-child img{aspect-ratio:1.35}}
.intro>* ,.opening>* ,.blueprint>* ,.reading>* ,.warmth>* ,.outcome>*{min-width:0}
